WEBVTT

00:00:10.430 --> 00:00:10.630
Is it an airplane?

00:00:11.160 --> 00:00:12.560
No, it's Superman!

00:00:15.300 --> 00:00:25.910
Superman, the giant of the Arctic.

00:00:54.030 --> 00:00:57.060
more powerful than a locomotive

00:00:58.530 --> 00:00:59.910
makes buildings jump with speed

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:06.640
In a single jump, this fantastic alien from the planet Krypton, the Man of Steel, Super-Man!

00:01:07.040 --> 00:01:18.750
The owner of an incredible physical strength, the Super-Man fights incessantly for truth and justice, disguised as a shy newspaper reporter, Clark Kent.

00:01:23.830 --> 00:01:29.780
Founding itself in the frozen desert of the arctic plains, an archaeological expedition in search of fossils...

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:32.200
makes a surprising discovery.

00:01:32.540 --> 00:01:35.140
A huge monster was found

00:01:35.140 --> 00:01:37.060
with the same appearance as when it wandered

00:01:37.060 --> 00:01:39.040
through the earth millions of years ago

00:01:39.040 --> 00:01:40.260
in the Mesozoic era,

00:01:40.260 --> 00:01:42.500
preserved in ice in perfect condition.

00:01:44.720 --> 00:01:47.080
Damaged by the difficult climatic conditions,

00:01:47.300 --> 00:01:48.680
scientists and their team

00:01:48.680 --> 00:01:50.140
of tireless workers

00:01:50.140 --> 00:01:53.140
manage to remove the gigantic creature from the site.

00:01:53.340 --> 00:01:55.200
The frozen monster

00:01:55.200 --> 00:01:56.800
is carried by a large revocator

00:01:56.800 --> 00:01:59.560
equipped with special refrigeration devices

00:01:59.560 --> 00:01:59.960
Subtitles by the Amara.org community

00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:00.860
brought to this country.

00:02:01.920 --> 00:02:04.840
Here, in a hall of the Museum of Natural History specially built,

00:02:05.220 --> 00:02:08.340
the scary creature is shown to the public for the first time.

00:02:11.070 --> 00:02:13.270
Tyrannosaurus. Habitat Siberia.

00:02:24.070 --> 00:02:25.010
Daily Planet.

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:35.260
So it means that if they allow the ice to melt, there is a possibility that the monster is still alive.

00:02:36.280 --> 00:02:37.140
Thank you, professor.

00:02:38.670 --> 00:02:38.990
Boss?

00:02:39.380 --> 00:02:41.800
Lois, there is a new angle in the history of the frozen monster.

00:02:41.980 --> 00:02:43.740
Go to the museum and see what they are doing.

00:02:44.100 --> 00:02:45.160
He is in a special refrigerator.

00:02:46.390 --> 00:02:47.020
Right, boss.

00:02:53.030 --> 00:02:54.990
Hey, Lois, do you want me to go with you there?

00:02:55.270 --> 00:02:56.410
Oh no, thank you.

00:02:56.770 --> 00:02:58.530
You will faint if you see the monster.

00:02:58.810 --> 00:02:59.690
You get scared easily.

00:03:02.110 --> 00:03:05.370
Maybe she's right, but the superman never fainted.

00:03:11.160 --> 00:03:13.660
This produces the necessary cooling.

00:03:13.980 --> 00:03:17.080
The control panel is down there, I'll show you.

00:03:18.570 --> 00:03:20.770
The entire facility is operated from this panel.

00:03:21.650 --> 00:03:25.050
It is necessary to observe the thermometer constantly,

00:03:25.410 --> 00:03:28.290
because any rise in temperature can be dangerous.

00:03:45.000 --> 00:03:45.840
Wow! What a story!

00:04:00.000 --> 00:04:00.560
Danger!

00:04:14.540 --> 00:04:17.070
Walk faster, please. Use the nearest exit.

00:04:19.660 --> 00:04:20.420
Control room.

00:04:20.500 --> 00:04:23.200
Please, keep walking. We have to evacuate this room immediately.

00:04:23.540 --> 00:04:23.920
What does he think?

00:04:32.080 --> 00:04:32.420
Police, please!

00:04:33.360 --> 00:04:35.380
Hello, boss!

00:04:35.520 --> 00:04:36.730
Send the platoon of shock!

00:04:36.930 --> 00:04:37.690
We are in trouble!

00:04:49.880 --> 00:04:52.080
Planet, call the municipal editor, now!

00:05:30.000 --> 00:05:30.960
Come back here in a few hours.

00:05:31.560 --> 00:05:34.260
Attention, all cars, head to Fifth Avenue right now.

00:05:34.700 --> 00:05:37.880
The monster of the Arctic runs enraged through the city.

00:05:38.960 --> 00:05:40.400
Chief, Lois is in the museum.

00:05:40.840 --> 00:05:41.860
Then I'll go there, Chief.

00:05:44.100 --> 00:05:46.020
This is a job for the super-man.

00:06:22.460 --> 00:06:24.460
It is better to return to the newsroom where the robbery is.

00:06:24.460 --> 00:06:25.460
There is still work to be done.

00:06:25.460 --> 00:06:26.460
Yes, my dear.

00:06:26.780 --> 00:06:28.780
And lose the best subject of the year?

00:06:28.780 --> 00:06:29.780
Never!

00:07:30.000 --> 00:07:30.520
I'll see you next time.

00:07:46.850 --> 00:07:47.470
Us!

00:07:49.600 --> 00:07:57.010
And this time behave.

00:07:57.800 --> 00:07:59.340
Yes, my boss. Thank you.

00:08:01.052 --> 00:08:04.052
Subtitles by the Amara.org community

00:08:06.268 --> 00:08:10.868
Daily Planet. Superman dominates the Arctic monster and avoids the destruction of the city.

00:08:11.676 --> 00:08:14.036
Monster in public exhibition in the zoo.

00:08:15.164 --> 00:08:17.864
You showed a lot of courage to get this paper, Lois.

00:08:17.864 --> 00:08:19.444
Thank you. Where were you?

00:08:19.612 --> 00:08:20.612
Me?

00:08:20.700 --> 00:08:22.900
Ah, I must have fainted.
